from lb import e
E=[
e("Book 12 - Summary (the System, prime avatar, Boko, Cyrion, Earth return)",["Book 12","the System Jason","prime avatar","Boko assassination","Cyrion System withdrawal","Jason returns to Earth","Jota Withers pirates"],
"""BOOK 12 (~16-17 years after Jason left Earth for Pallimustus; ~20-21 years after he first arrived on Pallimustus): Jason wakes seven hours after sitting on the Cosmic Throne; the GABs have left; his interface is now the System available to all essence-users. His true body is a universe (a single planetary system with Arbour as the only developed city; a space station shaped like his head is his seat). He needs a prime avatar; he strips reality-core power from vampires in his Saint-Étienne domain (the 'Bleed for me' purge) and from Death gets back his stored resurrection power. The prime avatar (nature: prime avatar of an astral nexus) has the gifts Prime Avatar, Numen, System Administrator, Sacred Phoenix, Relics of the King and Palanquin. He visits Rexion (brightheart city), Carlos saves Gibson Amouz, Farrah becomes an immortal Defier of the Will, Cloudweaver (the flask maker) tests him, Danielle becomes his political advisor, Anna Tilden is recruited, a Segurado messenger attack gets him called 'the Heretic King'. In Boko an assassin's Lesser Celestial Gorger drains him, Boko (~90,000 people) is evacuated, and a messenger host is annihilated by the ghost-fire phoenix; Jamis Fran Muskar agrees to free all messengers in occupied territories. Jason withdraws the System from slave-law regions after Cyrion's nobles hold Earthlings hostage. 74 Earthlings are gathered; the Sky Link bridge is calibrated; Jason makes a Burning Violet attempt; sails to Earth, defeats Jota Withers's pirates at the Australian Dimensional Artefact Site and reunites with Emi. Ends with 'Hey, Moppet.'""",12),
e("Prime Avatar, Numen and System Administrator",["prime avatar","Prime Avatar","Numen","System Administrator","Palanquin","Sacred Phoenix gift","Relics of the King","Astral Nexus","astral nexus"],
"""Jason's prime avatar (Book 12): a physical+spiritual gestalt with no soul of its own, an anchor for his transcendent power; made from reality material (naked, hairless, template adjusted for gold). Nature: Prime Avatar of an Astral Nexus (a nexus of astral kings, GABs and gods). Inherent gifts: Prime Avatar; Numen (divine aspects: establish spiritual domains; Akashic Speech; strip and transform remnant magic from killed magic entities; immune to rank suppression and detection/tracking/assessment; negate aura-related abilities by suppressing the user's aura); System Administrator (all System aspects, maps, voice/image chat, party/raid, assess; grant extras; access others' interfaces with permission or after suppressing their aura); Relics of the King (limited astral throne, gate, soul forge; stabilise dimensional spaces; exceed portal limits at cost; suppress spiritual manipulation); Sacred Phoenix (afflictions can add Ghost Fire; on lethal damage become a ghost fire phoenix; 1-year cooldown reduced by absorbing life force); Palanquin (Shade/Colin/Gordon forms of transport). Avatar death costs only time (a 'quarter-century time-out'); it cannot leave his domain... (later it does on Earth).""",12),
e("Akashic Speech and the Old Language",["Akashic Speech","divine voice","old language","words of creation","everyone hears own language"],
"""Akashic Speech: the voice of vessels of gods and astral beings; understood by all things capable of communication as if the soul were listening; everyone hears it in their own language. Jason's speech is now in the 'old language' (used by his sword's name and the Mark of Sin brand). Carlos notices his speech carries authority. His prime avatar is a 'hole in the universe'.""",12),
e("Saint-Etienne Vampire Purge (Book 12)",["Bleed for me purge","Saint-Etienne purge","reality core vampires","vampire purge Jason","blood rain"],
"""To make a prime avatar, Jason strips reality-core power from vampires: a giant nebulous eye in the sky of Saint-Étienne drives vampires, ghouls and blood servants mad; incantations: 'BLEED FOR ME', 'YOUR BLOOD IS NOT YOURS TO KEEP, BUT MINE ON WHICH TO FEAST', 'MINE IS THE JUDGEMENT, AND THE JUDGEMENT IS DEATH'. Blood mist is drawn into the eye; shadow arms drain; blood rain of gold-silver-blue motes explodes ghouls; ghost flame cleans up. Only vampires who consumed reality-core-infused blood lose it. Nigel Thornton witnesses. The same purge occurs in Slovakia; the blood farm there is liberated; Jason says 'This is who I am when I have to be.'""",12),
e("Nigel Thornton (gold)",["Nigel Thornton","Thorny gold","Nigel's team","Orange Darce Higgy Digit Woolzy Cobbo Jonno Green"],
"""Nigel 'Thorny' Thornton: first gold-ranker outside the US to reach gold without cores; leads a nine-person ex-Network paramilitary team (Orange, Darce, Higgy, Digit, Woolzy, Cobbo, Jonno, Green; mostly silver, core-users), contract operatives for Anna Tilden, spying on former Asano land at Saint-Étienne; wants to join Clan Asano; Rufus liberates a blood farm with him. Jason offers to ask Yumi to take them. Nigel later is Anna's close friend and joins the clan.""",12),
e("Rexion and Outer Rexion",["Rexion","Outer Rexion","The Ring Rexion","brightheart city","Fiorella","Bernice","Marla Rexion","Lorenn council leader"],
"""Rexion: the brightheart city named after the Cardinas rebuild; Lorenn is still Council Leader; Marla is military leader (molten-steel hair/eyes; asks 'Did you eat that mountain shaped like your head?'); Fiorella (militia) escorts Jason; Bernice (silver-haired metal-aspect customs attendant) makes Jason queue for papers; Outer Rexion is a town in the second (messenger-dug) shaft with a subterranean 'Las Vegas' ring and a Worship Ring (statue of Gary as a leonid hero). The portal had closed for a few years (while his aura vanished) and reopened. Population grew via Church of Fertility children and trade; Jason withdraws dominion over parts of the city so temples can be built; the city's astral space contains a messenger birthing planet producing elemental 'children, not corrupted' in a kilometres-tall tree (sealed). Lorenn: Jason says 'Fame isn't a prize, it's a price.' Statue of Gary exists.""",12),
e("Death returns the resurrection power",["Death returns resurrection","resurrection power returned","Jason time-out","Death temple Rexion"],
"""In Book 12 Ch8 the goddess Death returns the stored resurrection power Jason traded ('I will return what was taken now that it cannot be used for its original purpose'); he may build a Death temple in Rexion regardless. Jason is fully immortal now: no conditional resurrections; prime avatar replaceable.""",12),
e("Carlos saves Gibson Amouz",["Gibson Amouz saved","Carlos procedure","tainted magic cut out","Carlos Quilido Book 12"],
"""Carlos Quilido's procedure (Ch9): physically manifest the tainted Order of Redeeming Light magic and cut it out; 7 hours; Jason suppresses death/pain; dark single-eyed avatars assist; Jason absorbs the avatar's decade-plus memories. Gibson (son of Cassin Amouz, whose wealth funded the research) is saved. Carlos's research (~15+ years): vampirism cure works only for lesser vampires. Melody Jain is treated later with Arabelle and Neil (success).""",12),
e("Cloudweaver",["Cloudweaver","cloud flask maker","flask maker diamond","Cloudweaver they"],
"""Cloudweaver (they/them): diamond-rank gender-fluid shape-shifter, maker of the cloud flask, waited ~two decades; the diamond community sent them to test whether to 'put Jason down'; Jason pulled the flask into his soul, pushing out their back-door control. Cloudweaver upgrades the flask with Travis's weapons; works with Clive and Travis at the MRA. 'Diamond-rankers go to war; only they survive.'""",12),
e("Magical Research Association (MRA)",["Magical Research Association","MRA","Lorelei Grantham","Magic Research Association","Clive Archchancellor"],
"""Magical Research Association (MRA): open-access research body founded by Clive Standish (Archchancellor) with Vice Chancellor Lorelei Grantham (female; likes Clive), assistant Jeff; rivals the Magic Society; runs sky/satellite comms and a transportation network; Yaresh branch has a test facility and mirage-chamber operations (Munsen apprentice artificer; supervisor Roberto 'Bob'). Clive throws spies through the ceiling (Mickel, Herbert Norris ex-Vice-Dean of Alchemy). Clive's aura-analysis headband replicates Jason's interface.""",12),
e("Sky Link Company and Sea of Storms island",["Sky Link Company","sky link","Sea of Storms island","Travis Noble island","water link"],
"""Sky Link Company (Farrah and Travis): global telecommunications by relay towers and storm accumulators; headquartered in the Storm Kingdom; owns the uninhabited island in the Sea of Storms (colourful town, windmill-like accumulators) with the Builder's hidden infrastructure excavated and sealed; the underground ritual stones there calibrate the Pallimustus end of the bridge to Earth (needs Jason; stable usable bridge after ~a decade). Competes with the Magic Society's water link. Mariska Headingway threatened by Travis in the Cyrion arc ('reason eighty-seven').""",12),
e("Farrah chooses Defier of the Will",["Defier of the Will","Voice of the Will Farrah","Refuge island","Farrah immortal","half-ascended Astral Nexus"],
"""On Refuge (Jason's island in his planet: beach, over-water bungalows, rainforest, waterfalls; no powers work, speed/strength capped; Shade bartends) Farrah's window says Jason has half-ascended to Astral Nexus and offers VOICE OF THE WILL (access to his power, subject to dictates) or DEFIER OF THE WILL (negate the Astral Nexus's influence; he cannot harm her; can negate his prime avatar and isolate areas within his domains but not the astral kingdom; immortal; no access to his power). Farrah accepts Defier (Ch22: asleep, immortal, still silver, a step or two from gold). Jason dubs the bond not a familiar link.""",12),
e("Danielle Geller as political advisor",["Danielle advisor","Danielle diplomacy","Time Witch of Vitesse","diplomacy is war"],
"""Danielle Geller (the 'Time Witch of Vitesse') becomes Jason's political advisor on Earth ('do the opposite of every instinct'; 'diplomacy is war'); advises an org chart; her husband is Keith Geller. Dominion advised Jason: 'king or god'. Jason's objective: use power for problems others can't/won't, with trusted help (a Justice League-style think tank).""",12),
e("Dominion's advice and Projection Command: Presence",["Projection Command Presence","Dominion hegemony itself","no divine right of kings","Dominion temple Rexion"],
"""Dominion (god) tells Jason: 'I am not a ruler; I am the very concept of ruling... not a hegemon but hegemony itself'; 'there is no divine right of kings'; gives [Projection Command: Presence] (transcendent legendary consumable: control the presence of your transcendent power). On Earth: 'No half measures' - rule or stand above; 'try not to bring down civilisation'. Knowledge can peek into the prime avatar's head but not his true self.""",12),
e("Miguel Ladiv",["Miguel Ladiv","Vidal Ladiv nephew"],
"""Miguel Ladiv: Adventure Society shaft traffic official, nephew of Vidal Ladiv (deputy director of the Rimaros branch), drafted by Jason as Adventure Society liaison; afraid of transparent floors on Jason's cloud ship.""",12),
e("Prince Valdis duel and the Yaresh mirage arena",["Valdis duel","Shining Scabbard","Team Shining Scabbard","Sigrid Freyn Valdis husband","Mind's Eye Valdis"],
"""Team Shining Scabbard (Mirror Kingdom): leader/healer Sigrid Freyn and husband Prince Valdis (Mirror King's son; sword master; Mind's Eye, afterimage force constructs, Seeker Blade, Cross Slash, Blade Wave Barrage, Sword Soul absorbs afflictions). In the Yaresh mirage-chamber arena (commentators Ted and Ned; sponsor Barrington's Barrels) Jason's prime avatar fights Valdis: Midnight Eyes suppresses light; shadow arms hold daggers; Hegemony gives Sin to attackers; Punish, Leech Bite, Ruin; Cloak of Night gold becomes a portal to a dimensional space absorbing attacks; Valdis yields when Sword Soul empties. Sophie once beat Valdis by accelerating time. Other teams: Blood and Gold (Gabriel, Arabelle, Emir), Moon's Edge.""",12),
e("Segurado and the Heretic King",["Segurado","Millicent Marks","Heretic King","Navise Den Rigal","John Miller cook Segurado"],
"""Segurado (Uruguay-equivalent small city-state): messengers with summons (eyes in metal rings, bone cubes with mouths, cages of arms) attack; General Millicent Marks (elven gold wind caster) is saved when Jason's eye-shaped cloud ship (huge eyeball in dark red armour with satellite orbs shooting butterflies) arrives; messengers scream 'heretic king'. Jason poses as 'John Miller, team cook'. Navise Den Rigal (Voice of an Unorthodoxy astral king who had slipped Boris into Zell's service) is exposed.""",12),
e("Dragon Lands",["Dragon Lands","draconian prince","Zara draconian prince","fire realm"],
"""Dragon Lands (Antarctica-equivalent): draconian homeland with volcanoes, 'dragon mouth' geysers, apertures to a fire realm and the richest farmland (second-largest Greenstone export); xenophobic. Zara rebuffed a draconian prince (87th in line) who wanted her as fourth wife; Belinda imprisoned him; Zara put storm magic inside him.""",12),
e("Greenstone visit (Book 12)",["Greenstone Book 12","Madam Landry died","Jason statue bush","Vincent Trenslow Book 12","Hiram bronze"],
"""Greenstone ~15-20 years after Book 1: Madam Jennifer Landry died 7 years earlier; her daughters own 5 establishments. Elspeth Arella, still Adventure Society director, fears Jason's revenge; a statue of Jason is hidden behind a bush. Jason clears every delta contract overnight; visits Vincent Trenslow (immaculate moustache) in his bathrobe; Hiram (old, bronze) monitors the water aperture. Arrival ceremony features the Davone and Standish families. Adris Dorgan is Old City mayor. Li Li Mei is exposed as the mastermind of a rural 'folk-populist' movement.""",12),
e("Li Li Mei",["Li Li Mei","Li Mei","Mei honeypot","China honeypot"],
"""Li Li Mei: Chinese Earth refugee, silver core-user who ran a protection-racket-like populist manipulation of rural workers in low-magic zones for ~15 years to buy gold-rank monster cores; wants gold; careful aura control. Jason offers to take her to Earth and perhaps employ her; China sent her ~20 years earlier as a honey-trap look-alike. She helps Farrah gather Earthlings; Shade extracts her from Adventure Society interrogators (Glen Costling and Glennis).""",12),
e("Boko assassination and the ghost fire phoenix",["Boko","Boko evacuation","Lesser Celestial Gorger","ghost fire phoenix","The Hegemon has arisen","assassination attempt"],
"""In Boko (dark-skinned desert city; academic arts city north of Greenstone, ~90,000) a man in black-and-red armour stabs Jason with a slab sword (Lesser Celestial Gorger, gold uncommon; absorbs magic from gestalt entities by combining physical+spiritual energy; replica of a more sophisticated weapon) which drains his universe-power and paralyses his avatar. Jason lifts everyone out with his aura and drops them in the desert; Clive and company erect a containment ritual in Onslow's shell; four Voices of the Will of minor astral kings open portals above the city for 'an example'; Jason explodes silent; a perfect sphere of Boko is deleted (only temples remain, floating); System Alert: '[System Administrator] assassinated. The Hegemon has arisen. Beware his wrath.' The ghost fire phoenix (star-speckled dark bird with silver ghost flame) kills ~10,000 messengers. ~98% of Boko survived; hundreds to 2,000 died from his aura.""",12),
e("Jamis Fran Muskar's deal",["Jamis Fran Muskar deal","free all messengers","quarter million messengers","originals astral colossus","astral beast original"],
"""Jamis Fran Muskar (Council of Kings, copper hair, 7 ft, unwinged) tears open the messenger staging area, berates four kings for defying the Council's order not to provoke Jason, and offers Jason a Council seat. Originals (originators) are astral kings who weren't messengers: astral nexus (Jason), astral colossus (planet-sized prime avatar) and astral beast (armies of spawn creatures); messengers invented the 'originals' myth. Jason demands all messengers in occupied territories be freed to him (~quarter million, held in his kingdom); Jamis agrees to try; Jason vows a 'billion-year jihad' to unmake messenger society (burn birthing trees, free slaves). Jamis wants to become an original with the Purity artefact. Astrid Ela Dain (Voice of the Will) supports Jamis.""",12),
e("New Water and the Duke of Boko",["New Water","Duke Boko","Chief Inspector Krensler","diamond symbol badge","Adventure Society diamond badge"],
"""New Water: oasis city of sandstone and green stone with waterfalls built in days in Jason's soul realm for Boko's population; gods Dominion (framework for leadership), Hearth and Refuge will organise it; no aristocracy; Duke Boko (silver by cores, Kalar) is rebuked and banned. Chief Inspector Krensler (Continental Council, dark-skinned, bald) gives Jason a new Adventure Society badge: gold with a diamond symbol (treat by diamond-rank rules). Soramir suggested it; diamonds have 'more or less accepted' him.""",12),
e("Arash and Jamar",["Arash","Jamar","juice vendor Arash","blue-skinned vendor"],
"""Arash: blue-black, glowing-sigil runic juice vendor in Greenstone's Divine Square (Book 1) asks Jason to hire his nephew Jamar (bartender/kitchen manager; couldn't kill monsters); Jason attends Arash's family feast as John Miller.""",12),
e("Anna Tilden joins Jason (Book 12)",["Anna Tilden Book 12","Susan Tilden","Morris Manning","Patrick Clovis","Maël Baffier","Secretary Shu-Chen Lin"],
"""Anna Tilden (Under-Secretary-General at the UN Office of Supernatural Affairs, boss Secretary Shu-Chen Lin; wife Susan) flies to Saint-Étienne with security chief Morris Manning (US Dept of Supernatural Affairs), gold bodyguard Patrick Clovis and French delegate Maël Baffier; four-winged monsters attack the plane; Ketevan Arziani and Rufus greet them. After three days of Q&A with Jason (avatar in an apron who can't taste) she provisionally accepts the job as his political consultant. Jason says he could conquer the world and wants to avoid war. Susan: great astral beings are 'the thing that makes the car work'. Later Jason keeps her out of the pirate plan, then apologises; she lands with Rufus, Taika and Gary Sharpton at the Australian site and meets Lenora Coleman.""",12),
e("Saint-Etienne in Book 12 and Gary Sharpton",["Gary Sharpton","reincarnated Gary","leonid Gary teen","rune puzzle cube","Emi 22"],
"""Book 12 Saint-Étienne: cloud city with canals, parks, Renaissance admin tower; refugees with green scales and wings; Craig Vermillion lives in the Slovakian vampire astral space; Erika and Ian host picnics; Nigel's families joined. Emi (22ish) and Vincent (a boy) are friends of Gary Sharpton, the reincarnated leonid Gary (teenage mechanic/engineer, inventor of a saucer craft), who says 'Mr Asano is crazy awesome'. Terry Tilden is Anna's brother.""",12),
e("Cyrion",["Cyrion","Estercost capital","world engineer golems Cyrion","Geller compound Cyrion"],
"""Cyrion: capital of Estercost and largest city in the world (concentric walls with farmland; Tokyo-meets-Emerald City from the air); the Builder's cult attacked it before the messenger invasion (dormant world-engineer golems outside the walls, picked clean by Clive and Belinda); the Continental Council sits in Vitesse. Earthlings were housed in the Geller compound there. Noble houses use indenture laws as slave laws.""",12),
e("Earthlings gathered: Daryll and Koa",["Daryll","Koa","Earthlings 74","Earth refugees returned","Koa Ignite Stone"],
"""Of ~104 Earthlings pulled to Pallimustus, 53 sign up in Cyrion and 74 total return to Earth (~30 stay, are lost or dead). Daryll (Darryl): troll were-crocodile (fae) from Far North Queensland, Cabal member, only non-essence-user among them, blood magic (ropes, hammers, venom). Koa: Māori teen at the pull (mother worked for the Network, now for the Gellers), no cores; Absorb Electricity, Ignite Stone ('Let the heart of the world beat'). Stormspire drakes attack the northern mountain city; Nik leads a raid group; Danielle is raid leader; Jason's cloud ship takes configuration D20 (black icosahedron with eyes).""",12),
e("Cyrion nobles kidnapped; Sadi Andali",["Sadi Andali","Headingway","Patterson Kennington","Garret Headingway","Ben Headingway","Percival Headingway","Mariska Headingway","indenture"],
"""When Cyrion nobles use indenture law to hold Earth-people hostage, Jason sends letters ('promise to myself... wipe out slavery... not a negotiating position') and withdraws the System from slave-law regions with a one-day notice. Belinda (disguised as butler James) and the team poison-scone-kidnap seven nobles (Garret Headingway, Patterson Kennington...) and sell them in Sadi Andali's slave markets (lawless desert east of Estercost). Ben Headingway (top gold of House Headingway) leads raids; Brian, a gold priest of Dominion, buys Patterson to protect him ('Slavery is a petty tyranny; my lord looks higher'). Duke Percival Headingway and business manager Mariska decide to stop antagonising Jason.""",12),
e("Vandrick Macarro and diamond etiquette",["Vandrick","Vandrick Macarro","diamond etiquette","one world-changing action"],
"""Vandrick Macarro (diamond) arbitrates for the Queen of Estercost and says the diamond community considers the System Jason's to administer; diamond etiquette: stand alone, respect the mortal/immortal boundary (after ~500 years step back), everyone gets ONE great world-changing action (Jason's is abolishing slavery via the System). Young diamonds: Allayeth and Charist (Yaresh), Mirror King (Victor Volaire), Roland Remore (via proxies); older: Soramir Rimaros and Dawn (out in the cosmos). Pole slides in Jason's palace are labelled with team names.""",12),
e("Jacinta Adeline",["Jacinta Adeline","Cyrion Adventure Society director"],
"""Jacinta Adeline: Adventure Society Cyrion branch director, drinks with Danielle Geller; says Sophie Wexler is Jason's biggest supporter.""",12),
e("Jota Withers and Aractus Jakaar",["Jota Withers","Aractus Jakaar","Natala Spiro","Kreegle","Jakaar Fleet","pirates Interstice","cosmic pirates"],
"""Jota Withers: gold-rank captain from an Interstice feeder universe, working for pirate 'Admiral' Aractus Jakaar (fat, pointy hat, moustache; fleet that plunders low-magic worlds) with first officer Natala Spiro and mutineer Kreegle. The World-Phoenix opened Pallimustus' neighbour Earth to gold-rankers; the Earth secret council (US excluded) invited them to remove Jason, giving them a pretence under the Rules of Intrusion. Jota stays at Asano Village hosted by Noriko, concludes Jason is of consequence, surrenders his ship; Jason forfeits the ship, takes Jota and Natala prisoner (Arabelle interviews them) and the Jakaar mutineers are beaten. Jota reads Jason's System window: 'Prime Avatar (Astral Nexus) [System Administrator]'.""",12),
e("Rules of Intrusion",["Rules of Intrusion","intrusion rules","cosmic community open","declared open world"],
"""Rules of Intrusion: cosmic law (enforced by the restored Cosmic Throne, now rigid) on entering worlds that have not declared themselves open to the cosmic community; flexible before, rigid now. Invaders must fulfil the invitation's conditions (remove Jason) or violate the rules. Rufus: they mostly applied to holy wars on Pallimustus, but also govern dimensional invasion.""",12),
e("Dimensional Artefact Site One",["Dimensional Artefact Site One","Lenora Coleman","Barry Sinise","artefact city","Australian standing stones","Gordon Truffett prime minister"],
"""Dimensional Artefact Site One (the artefact city): ~9,000-person town around the Australian standing stones where Jason and Farrah vanished; hardened for 15 years by a multinational coalition; weapon bunkers with magical howitzers; run by Director of Operations Lenora Coleman (core-user bureaucrat), deputy Barry Sinise (mayor), assistant Cassie, Security Commander Higgins, Sub-Commander Keene; first director Gordon Truffett is now Australian PM. A Chinese bomber failed. Gold-rankers belong mostly to US and China; Lord Willoughby (English Network gold) and a Chinese gold-ranker are on roster.""",12),
e("Asano Noriko's village and Australian land seizure",["Asano Village hijack","Noriko Asano hosts Jota","true Asano clan Australia","eminent domain Asano land"],
"""After Jason's clan hid in Europe, the Australian government seized Asano Village and the stone-circle land by eminent domain and gave them to Asano Noriko's Japanese-line 'true Asano clan', allied with the Network faction; Noriko hosts Jota and dismisses the System link ('utter nonsense'). Jason's anger at Lenora: 'The rules of this world... mean that if you have the power, you can take what you like.'""",12),
e("Pirate battle at the Artefact City",["pirate battle Earth","Elenore Boatwell","Suck and Cut","Unstoppable Force Humphrey pirates","Jason Verdict rain"],
"""Jason's ship (>300 m, gold/silver/blue light arrival, dark red panels, ring of eye-orbs, gold lyric text on the side) vs the Jakaar pirate ship (~80 m); 23 mutineers (Kreegle's) attack; Jason blots out the sun, dons void-portal cloak and blood robes, spawns 200+ Shade bodies with black-red daggers; Hegemony suppresses 20+ aura powers; Inescapable harpoon blocks shadow jumps; the team (Biscuit + Farrah) arrives (Sophie's Eternal Moment for the team, Belinda's Force Tether, Farrah's Lava Cannon x2 via Mirror Magic, Clive's Wrath on Onslow, Humphrey's Unstoppable Force, Neil's Grand Renewal); Jason's Verdict rain annihilates; he spares pirates (prisoners go to his prison planet with surrendered messenger armies) and halts the dimension-jump with a ship-eye 'No.' Jota says the ship is a temple.""",12),
e("Lenora's confrontation and Jason meets Gary Sharpton",["Jason Lenora Coleman","mosquito swat","Gary Sharpton meets Jason"],
"""Jason (floral shirt, aura imperceptible then crushing) tells Lenora about the eminent-domain seizure ('You don't threaten a mosquito... you swat it'), refuses to care what governments want, and asks Anna to find a drop-off for returning refugees. He then meets Gary Sharpton ('named for a good friend') and recruits him to explore the pirate dimension ship. He reunites with Emi: 'Hey, Moppet.'""",12),
e("Burning Violet application",["Burning Violet application","Monica","Roland Remore Jason","Humphrey returns pins","enough rope protocol"],
"""Jason applies to the Burning Violet guild in Vitesse; receptionist Monica; Neiman Bassingthwaite warns of factions; Roland Remore arranged it as a lesson/trap to keep Jason out of his fight with 'the order'; Jason retorts 'power rules'; Team Biscuit withdraws; Victor Volaire (Mirror King) and Roland discuss; Roland says Jason has a sense of responsibility and 'deserves a break' until he must get involved.""",12),
e("Cassandra Mercer reunion",["Cassandra reunion","Cassandra Neil","Jiralla","Henrietta Geller team"],
"""Jason meets Cassandra Mercer in Vitesse (20 years later; she is near gold, teaming with Jiralla and Henrietta Geller); they talk about being adventurers ('puts themselves between the bad things and those needing protection'); Neil dumped her; she won't see Neil; Nik hopes to see her.""",12),
e("Springclaw gorillas and Team Biscuit's gold tactics",["Springclaw gorillas","double scoop slam","gold tactical playbook","Team Biscuit gold abilities"],
"""Team Biscuit's gold playbook (Book 12): Humphrey Mighty Strength (enlarges him), Dive Bomb; Sophie speed, healing aura, mirage afterimage implosions; Neil absorb-and-counter summon, Burst Shield; Belinda Instant Adept, Force Tether; Clive top single-target damage, buffs, Onslow battle platform; Zara concentrated storm; Stash tiny mouse that becomes a three-headed carrier. Springclaw gorillas (gold, cunning, anticoagulant venom) defeated by the 'double scoop slam'.""",12),
e("Zara Rimaros returns (Book 12)",["Princess Zara","Zara Rimaros Book 12","Lord Alberto","Storm King cousin","Trench Farrah"],
"""Zara restores her sapphire hair and role as Princess Zara Rimaros to abolish indentured servitude in the Storm Kingdom slowly; the Storm King is her brother Emiliano ('Stupid Emiliano'; also described as an adopted cousin; about a decade into his tenure) and her father has retired. At the Sky Link island Lord Alberto slights her and she threatens to peel him; Jason's delegation offer (40 people, no diamonds) is on the table. She and Jason have romantic tension (Helen of Troy story). Farrah's boyfriend Trench (Trenchant Moore) wants something serious.""",12),
e("Bridge to Earth and expedition members",["Earth expedition","Rimaros delegation","Zareen Rimaros","Storm Kingdom delegation","bridge activation"],
"""Jason's Earth expedition: Team Biscuit, Rimaros delegation (40, incl. Zareen, Liara's daughter), Valdis and Rick Geller with teams, Lorelei Grantham and MRA researchers, Travis and Farrah's employees, Jory with alchemists, clergy for Boko refugees in Jason's astral kingdom (cut off from gods), Gabrielle Pellin (now Travis's wife), Carlos, Melody (recovering), Earthlings. The bridge opens quietly; Jason's cloud ship ferries via the proto-bridge guide wire. Melody Jain wakes after treatment (Carlos soul, Arabelle mental, Neil body).""",12),
e("Gabrielle and Travis; Jory and Belinda",["Gabrielle Travis wife","Jory Belinda Book 12","Jory alchemists Earth"],
"""Gabrielle (priestess of Knowledge) is Travis Noble's wife and attends the Earth trip; Jason apologises for disrespecting Knowledge and recalls the tango. Jory travels with alchemists (awkward with Belinda).""",12),
e("Slovakian vampire astral space",["Slovakian vampire city","city with no dawn","vampires moon eclipse","sane vampires"],
"""Jason's Slovakian astral space holds a sunless Gothic city (Prague/Istanbul/Batman influences) where Earth's remaining sane vampires live. Craig Vermillion (gold after feeding on vampire lords; locked himself away for years) lives there. Jason plans to move them to a moon in his own solar system with a permanent eclipse where sunlight doesn't cause insanity. Jason intends to kill all remaining vampires outside.""",12),
e("Secret council of Earth and Americans' warning",["secret council Earth","Darius Shepherd","Michael Glasser","Earth powers oppose Jason","Indonesia opposes","Rules of Intrusion warning"],
"""Darius Shepherd (US Dept of Supernatural Affairs) and Michael Glasser (State Dept) warn Jason that a secret council of Earth's most powerful states and societies has hired outsiders to remove him; opposition: Australia, China, Indonesia, the UK; Russia and Africa are Cabal territory; Asia split; the US Network is reconciled with the US government and neutral/friendly; Network China (rebranded 'the Network') hates Jason; vampires are a wildcard. Taika, Shiro Asano and Wesley Asano (vehicle essence) escort them; Boris mediates.""",12),
e("Roland Remore",["Roland Remore","Roland","Remore patriarch","arch-chancellor Remore"],
"""Roland Remore: diamond-ranker, arch-chancellor of Remore Academy and Rufus's grandfather (bald, dark-skinned, looks 40, ~400 years old, sword master). Controls Burning Violet through proxies; in conflict with 'the order' (Order of the Reaper) and wanted Jason out of the fight. Rufus waited until 19 for essences.""",12),
e("Jason's gold-rank character sheet (Book 12 Appendix)",["Jason gold sheet","Jason 38% to diamond","Jason gold abilities list","Jason Appendix I"],
"""Jason Asano (Book 12): Nature Prime Avatar of an Astral Nexus; Gold; 38% to diamond. Attributes Power(Blood) G3, Speed(Dark) G4, Spirit(Doom) G3, Recovery(Sin) G3. Essences Dark/Blood/Sin/Doom. Dark: Midnight Eyes G5, Cloak of Night G5, Path of Shadows G4, Hand of the Reaper G4, Shadow of the Hegemon G4. Blood: Blood Harvest G3, Leech Bite G4, Feast of Blood G4, Sanguine Horror G4, Haemorrhage G4. Sin: Punish G4, Feast of Absolution G3, Sin Eater G3, Hegemony G5, Castigate G4. Doom: Inexorable Doom G4, Punition G4, Blade of Doom G3, Verdict G4, Avatar of Doom G4.""",12),
e("Jason's gold abilities (Appendix III)",["gold ability Midnight Eyes","Cloak of Night gold","Path of Shadows gold","Hand of the Reaper gold","Shadow of the Hegemon bodies","Thief of Life","Thief of Spirit","Exsanguination","Blood Glutton"],
"""Gold effects: Midnight Eyes diminishes light sources; Hand of the Reaper more arms, further away, armed with conjured weapons; Cloak of Night becomes a void portal (extreme ongoing mana); Path of Shadows global portals; Shadow of the Hegemon 211 bodies as aura beacons; Blood Harvest gains Strength of My Enemies/Endless Power; Leech Bite inflicts Thief of Life; Haemorrhage Exsanguination; Feast of Blood Blood Glutton; Sanguine Horror can exceed mass limits; Punish Thief of Spirit; Castigate's Mark of Sin resists cleanse; Feast of Absolution gives allies Resistant+Integrity; Sin Eater consumes allies' curses/diseases/poisons over time; Hegemony no longer splits strength; Inexorable Doom accelerates; Doom Blade sword extra damage per Legacy of Sin; Punition AoE variant; Verdict wide-area; Avatar of Doom butterflies create seeking clouds.""",12),
e("Stash's letter and Stash",["Stash letter","Velitraxistaasch","Pastry Stash","Stash 22","Stash baker"],
"""Stash (Velitraxistaasch), mirage dragon, now ~22¾ years old (home-schooled; hill mouse form in Humphrey's pocket 'chu'; runs The Pastry Stash patisserie in Vitesse; caused flour-silo fires; calls Humphrey 'Da Humphrey'; Gary was best at scratching behind his ears). Wrote Jason a letter (Ch0). Mother is Carlivexistrix.""",12),
e("Ketevan Arziani and Asano clan organisation",["Ketevan Arziani Book 12","Asano clan org chart","Clan economy contribution points","clan contribution points"],
"""Clan Asano (Earth): matriarch Yumi; chief of staff Ketevan Arziani; economy: spirit coins or clan contribution points; basics free (food, lodging, transport, healing, simple clothing), extras cost points; schools; essences sold for points (Jason left supply). Most members are essence-users; confluence combos are unreliable (variety returning). Honorary members: Rufus.""",12),
e("Jason's physical universe",["Jason's universe","head space station","observation lounge eye","Jason planet"],
"""Jason's true body is a universe (single planetary system; blazing sun; habitable Earth-like planet with only Arbour developed; orbital space station shaped like his head with the observation lounge as its eye serving as seat of power, relic reliquary and entry point for dimension-faring visitors). No one can enter without his allowance. His astral kingdom is smaller than the Builder's but immortal. Refuge is an island on that planet.""",12),
e("Humphrey and Sophie in Book 12",["Humphrey Sophie wedding","Humphrey gold","Sophie gold Book 12","Hump engaged"],
"""Sophie (gold; wind blades, stonehide lizard herds) reunites with Humphrey (rainbow-scale armour, bomb drops) when Clive summons her to Yaresh; they are engaged. Jason jokingly challenges Humphrey to a duel for her hand.""",12),
e("Neil and Nik after Book 11",["Neil Nik","Neil Mirror Kingdom","Nik Dad","Nik Team Shining Scabbard"],
"""Neil and Nik (Jason's son, now silver, calls Jason 'Dad') travel with Team Shining Scabbard in the Mirror Kingdom. Neil ghosted Cassandra 10 years ago; he is 'moping about some girl'. Nik asks for a hug; Jason can't make more Lehenik until at full power; told his sister and grandmother about Nik. Nik later organises the raid group at Cyrion.""",12),
e("Death Pact consequences Book 12",["Keeper of the Cycle Book 12","Death temple","resurrection Jason Book 12"],
"""Death returns the resurrection power so Jason's prime avatar can be replaced; his pact still prevents him from resurrecting others. Gods cannot enter his dominion; Jason withdraws dominion from parts of Rexion and New Water so temples can be built. Ex-Purity priests (stasis-held centuries, released ~20 years ago) petition for residency; Jason refuses 'Lord/messiah'.""",12),
e("Gold monsters of Book 12 (tactics)",["stormspire drake","Sadi Andali slave market","River Table"],
"""Stormspire drakes: school-bus-sized rock-and-lightning dragons (silver; two gold) attacking the northern mountain city; River Table: vast flatland crossed by waterways, once a mountain range, last Earthling pickup site.""",12),
]
